extracted = ""
i = 0
for d in context:
    i = i + 1
    q = "You are given one document. Extract any information relevant to the following story and provide it in a compact, structured way.\n\nStory we are matching:\n- Year: 2019, country: England\n- During a match, a home-team player squirted a water bottle at an away player, starting a scuffle\n- The away team finished with: 6 shots on goal (aka shots on target), 4 yellow cards, and 4 corner kicks\n- The away player who was squirted was on loan at the away club from another club (the parent club)\n- That parent club had a European match (UEFA competition) where this player featured on the bench\n\nWhat to extract (include if present; skip if not in the document):\nCandidate:\nPlayer: <name>\nLoan club (away team): <club>\nParent club (loaned from): <club>\nMatch: <date>, <competition>, <home> vs <away>, <venue if stated>\nIncident: <1-2 sentences with brief quotes>\nAway team stats: <shots on goal/on target, yellow cards, corner kicks>\nEuropean bench appearance: <parent club> vs <opponent>, <competition>, <date> (on bench)\nEvidence quotes:\n- \"<quote 1>\"\n- \"<quote 2>\"\n\nOnly output a Candidate block if the document contains at least one of: the water-bottle incident, the player identity, the loan/parent clubs, or the European bench appearance detail. If it is irrelevant, output nothing.\n\nBEGIN_DOCUMENT\n" + d + "\nEND_DOCUMENT"
    r = llm_query(q)
    extracted = extracted + "\n---\nDoc#" + str(i) + ":\n" + r

final_q = "You will be given multiple Candidate blocks compiled from various documents. Using only those candidates and their evidence quotes, answer this:\n\nQuestion: What was the name of the team that the bench appearance was against? (This refers to the opponent in the European match for the parent club of the player involved in the 2019 England match where a home player squirted a water bottle at him, starting a scuffle. The away team in that match had 6 shots on goal, 4 yellow cards, and 4 corner kicks.)\n\nInstructions:\n- Identify the correct player and match if possible.\n- Prefer candidates that explicitly mention the water-bottle incident and the 2019 England match, and, if available, the away-team stats matching 6 shots on goal, 4 yellows, 4 corners.\n- Then extract the opponent of the European bench appearance for his parent club.\n- Output ONLY the opponent team's name, nothing else.\n\nCANDIDATES:\n" + extracted + "\n\nAnswer (opponent team name only):"
ans = llm_query(final_q)
return_result(ans.strip())